WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:06.480
Now that we have covered arrangement of digits,

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:08.640
let's try arranging people.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.980
Say we have five people.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.440
And we have just three chairs.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:17.180
The chairs are placed in a row or in a straight line.

00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.760
Five people and three chairs.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.000
With this situation, in how many ways do you think

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.720
can these chairs be occupied?

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.780
Now if you've gone through our previous sessions

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.080
on forming numbers,

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.980
you should quickly realize that this problem is not too different.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.840
Five people is analogous to five different digits.

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:41.100
And three chairs are analogous to the three slots,

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.580
for the three digit number we had to form.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.000
Correct!

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.460
If you remember,

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.240
we were given five digits

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.320
and asked for the number of three digit numbers we can form.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.680
Here we have been given five people

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:56.780
and have been asked for the number of ways

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.260
in which we can arrange any three of them

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:00.960
on these three chairs.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.000
It's exactly the same.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.080
Just that they have used chairs and people

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:07.800
instead of numbers and digits.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.260
So assume that these three chairs are like three slots.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.680
In how many ways can we fill the first slot?

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.580
Understand the question well.

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:20.640
If we have five people and all three chairs are empty.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:24.100
In how many ways can the first chair be occupied?

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:25.660
It's logic!

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.140
Any one of the five people can be seated on this chair.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:30.460
It's obvious!

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:33.680
The chair can be occupied in five ways.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.600
So out of the five people,

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:38.640
one person is seated on the first chair now.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.120
Now one person having taken the seat,

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.080
in how many ways can the second chair be occupied?

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:46.360
One person is seated here.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:50.660
It means one of the five people is seated on the first chair.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:54.980
And any one of the remaining four can be seated on the second.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.000
Once the first chair is occupied,

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.920
the second chair can be filled in four ways.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.960
You should be able to answer the next question.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.740
Assuming one person is seated on the first chair,

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.380
and another on the second,

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:10.300
in how many ways can the third chair be occupied?

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:16.540
It's easy.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.440
Two out of the five are seated on the first two chairs.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.280
Only three remain.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:24.020
If one person is seated on the first chair

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.700
and another on the second,

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.520
then the third chair can be occupied by any one

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.460
of the remaining three people.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:31.820
Three ways.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:35.580
In our first session based on permutations and combinations,

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.720
we discussed the two important rules of counting.

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:42.980
'And' is multiplication 'Or' is addition.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:46.240
So do we multiply these or add them?

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:49.920
To know the answer just read out what you have solved.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.940
Will it be filling the first or the second or the third chair?

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:58.080
Or will it be filling the first and the second and the third chair?

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.700
Of course it will be 'and'.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:04.640
We need to look at the ways in which all three chairs are occupied.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.100
So we multiply these ways.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.960
And we get the answer as 60 ways.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.640
If there are five people,

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.340
then there are 60 ways

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:15.800
in which these three chairs can be occupied.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.660
Let me modify the question a bit.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:20.900
This time we have five people,

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:24.000
and we have been provided with five chairs.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.380
Again the chairs are in a row.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.840
In how many ways can the chairs be occupied?

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:31.400
What does this mean?

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:34.200
In simple words the question is asking us

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:38.680
for all possible arrangements of five people on these five chairs.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.580
Again, let's take these five chairs as five slots.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:47.220
And using our usual technique, let's go slot by slot.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.740
In how many ways can the first chair be occupied?

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:54.520
Any one of the five people can be seated on the first chair.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.460
So there are five different ways,

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.280
in which the first chair can be occupied.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:01.660
Understand the situation now.

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:04.820
One of these five is seated on the first chair.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:06.360
Once this has happened,

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:09.440
in how many ways can the second chair be occupied?

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:11.600
As there are four people remaining,

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:14.560
one of those four can be seated on the second chair.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:18.040
The second chair can be occupied in four ways.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.480
Once these two chairs are occupied,

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:23.420
the third one can be occupied in three ways.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:26.580
And similarly, two ways for the fourth chair,

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:29.620
and just one person remains for the fifth one.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:32.460
One way in which the fifth chair can be occupied,

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.660
if four people are seated in the initial four.

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.280
And to get the answer,

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:39.580
we multiply these ways.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.780
Five times four is 20,

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.940
20 times 3 is 60,

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:47.140
and 60 times 2 is 120.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.560
120 ways is the answer.

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:55.960
120 ways in which five people can occupy five chairs.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:59.540
This is also equal to five factorial.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.360
Now books would ask you to memorise this.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:06.400
Arranging five people on five chairs as five factorial.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:10.640
Or 'N people' on 'N chairs' as 'N factorial'.

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:12.980
But don't memorise this.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:17.500
You have to understand how we arrived at a 5 factorial.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:19.260
After watching this video,

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.360
I am sure you've understood why.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:24.340
But if this video was a little too fast for you,

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:25.840
please go through it again

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.480
as many questions are built around this concept.

